@startuml

start

:Thermal management controller executes as state machine on RTOS;
fork
  :Govern PWM fans;
fork again
  :Govern liquid-cooling pump duty cycles;
end fork

:Multi-source fault condition triggered by deviations in;
fork
 :Temperature;
fork again
 :Pressure;
fork again
 :Humidity;
fork again
 :System rail voltage from PMIC;
fork again
 :RF signal strength;
fork again
 :Data uplink rate;
end fork

:Activate level-1 fault handler;
:Initiate concurrent tasks;

fork
:High-priority ISR;
:Real-time environmental monitoring;
fork again
:Medium-priority task using a watchdog;
:Cyclic equipment status checks;
fork again
:Lower-priority thread via mutex-protected priority queue;
:Continuous system load assessment and resource optimization;
end fork

:Level-2 fault management routine;
:Spawn parallel operations;

fork
:Cyclically probe CAN bus link state with CRC verification;
fork again
:Asynchronously record structured audit logs to ring buffer;
:Flush to non-volatile storage within I/O budget limits;
fork again
:Periodically evaluate system performance envelope;
fork again
:Update fault diagnosis report;
end fork

:Sensor fusion and calibration routines execute periodically;
if(Persistent out-of-range reading?) then(yes)
:Engage system redundancy;
:Invoke controlled cool-down protocol managed by FADEC/BMS;
:Employ exponential backoff for retry operations;
else(no)
end if

stop

@enduml
